944:
This chapter sets forth the standards which shall control the number, type, and placement of signs within the unincorporated portion of Whitfield County, upon individual lots, parcels, structures, or accessory structures. The purposes of such standards set forth in this chapter include the following:
(1) To maintain and to enhance the aesthetic environment and natural beauty of Whitfield County, while balancing those interests with support for positive economic development of Whitfield County;
(2) To maintain and to improve traffic safety;
(3) To minimize potential confusion created as a result of size, location, construction, or manner of display of signs;
(4) To minimize potential adverse effects of signs upon neighboring properties;
(5) To maintain and to enhance the tranquility and compatibility of uses within low density residential areas, while balancing those interests with the rights of such homeowners to communicate freely; and
(6) To encourage the necessary and proper use of signs as a means of effective and Constitutionally protected communication.
(Ord. No. 2015-0810, § 2, 8-10-15)

